<header><p class="st-kicker">caliphate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Caliphate of Ibn al-Zubayr</h1><p class="st-meta">683 CE – 692 CE · capital Mecca</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A rival caliphate based in Mecca that, during the Second Fitna, was recognised across much of the Islamic world before the Umayyads crushed it.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-allah-ibn-al-zubayr">Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr</a>, son of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/companions-of-the-prophet">Companion of the Prophet</a> and grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-bakr-al-siddiq">Abu Bakr</a>, refused to recognise the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazid-i">Yazid I</a> and took refuge in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>. When Yazid died in 683 and his son soon after, Ibn al-Zubayr proclaimed himself caliph and was accepted in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hejaz">Hejaz</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-yemen">Yemen</a> and much of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>He governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, where he rebuilt the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaaba">Kaaba</a> after it was damaged in an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad</a> siege, while his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musab-ibn-al-zubayr">Mus'ab</a> ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basra">Basra</a>. His authority depended on governors and tribal allies, and he faced revolts from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kharijites">Kharijites</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/najdiyya">Najdiyya</a> and from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mukhtar-al-thaqafi">al-Mukhtar</a>'s pro-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alids">Alid</a> movement at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kufa">Kufa</a>, which Mus'ab defeated in 687.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad</a> victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-marj-rahit-684">Marj Rahit</a> in 684 kept <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a>, Marwan I retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in 685, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-malik-ibn-marwan">Abd al-Malik</a> reconquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musab-ibn-al-zubayr">Mus'ab</a> was killed in 691. In 692 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-hajjaj-ibn-yusuf">al-Hajjaj</a> besieged and bombarded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-allah-ibn-al-zubayr">Ibn al-Zubayr</a> died fighting and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> was reunited.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/caliphate-of-ibn-al-zubayr.jpg" alt="Caliphate of Ibn al-Zubayr" width="320" height="324"><figcaption>Image: Not credited · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Silver_dirham_of_Abd_Allah_ibn_al-Zubayr_690-91.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>683 CE – 692 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>caliphate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mecca</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a>, <a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Zubayrid Caliphate, Zubayrids</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=688&amp;focus=caliphate-of-ibn-al-zubayr" aria-label="Caliphate of Ibn al-Zubayr on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5750 1386 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Caliphate of Ibn al-Zubayr lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6070 1642L6134 1224"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6134 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6070 1642h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6070 1642h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mecca. <a href="/atlas?year=688&amp;focus=caliphate-of-ibn-al-zubayr">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
